<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Where a rider sits on a penguin, for Giddy-Up.

       The original of this patch never fired, for three separate reasons. It guarded on a mod
       called "Giddy-up! Core", which no longer exists; it added a mod extension of class
       GiddyUpCore.DrawingOffsetPatch, which the 1.6 assembly no longer defines; and its xpath
       asked for a ThingDef named "King_penguin" when the def is king_penguin. defNames are
       case-sensitive, so that last one had never matched anything, in any version.

       It is also on the wrong animal. Giddy-Up 2 makes an animal mountable by default when
       race.baseBodySize is greater than 1.2 (GiddyUp.Setup), so the king penguin at 0.35 is not
       a mount and cannot become one without a GiddyUp.Mountable extension. The emperor penguin,
       at 1.35, is - and it is the one that has pack textures.

       The guard tests one of Giddy-Up's own defs rather than its display name: PatchOperationFindMod
       compares against ModMetaData.Name, an exact string that belongs to whoever is maintaining the
       fork this month. The extension class itself must stay inside <value>, which is an XmlContainer
       and is not resolved until the operation applies - a modExtension whose class cannot be found
       fails the whole def it was added to, penguin included. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ConceptDef[defName="GUC_Animal_Handling"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="emperor_penguin"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="GiddyUp.DrawingOffset">
          <!-- x sideways, y draw altitude, z vertical. The x and z are the author's own, carried
               over from the CSV form the old class used. The y was -1 there; Giddy-Up 2 ships 0
               for every one of the animals it offsets itself and settles draw order in the render
               nodes instead, so it is 0 here too. -->
          <northOffset>(0.00, 0.00, -0.50)</northOffset>
          <southOffset>(0.00, 0.00, -0.30)</southOffset>
          <eastOffset>(0.20, 0.00, -0.20)</eastOffset>
          <westOffset>(-0.20, 0.00, -0.20)</westOffset>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
